    <h2>What Is the Cotton Candy Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Cotton Candy Blizzard is the lightest of the Summer 2026 seasonal Blizzards. Cotton candy flavoring creates that distinctive airy, spun-sugar sweetness you recognize from the fairground version. Unlike the heavier <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's</a> or <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster</a>, this Blizzard is genuinely light — 460 cal for a Small is toward the lower end of the Blizzard calorie range.</p>
  <p>Find all Summer 2026 seasonal Blizzards and their prices on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Cotton Candy Blizzard — Good for Kids</h2>
  <p>The Cotton Candy Blizzard is one of the most kid-friendly seasonal offerings. The flavor is recognizable to anyone who has had cotton candy at a fair or amusement park. Combined with DQ soft serve and a fun pink-tinted swirl, it is visually appealing and sweet without being overpowering.</p>
  <p>For younger guests, the Mini ($4.49) is the right size. If ordering a full kids meal, the <a href="/categories/kids-meals">DQ Kids Meal</a> includes a vanilla cone — a Cotton Candy Blizzard Mini ordered separately is a good add-on treat.</p>
  <h2>Lowest-Calorie Summer 2026 Blizzard</h2>
  <p>At 460 cal (Small), the Cotton Candy Blizzard is the lightest-calorie option in the Summer 2026 seasonal lineup — lower than S'mores (500), Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake (540), and the <a href="/items/mixing-bowl-mashup-blizzard">Mixing Bowl Mashup</a> (520).</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cotton Candy Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>460</td><td>Lightest summer seasonal</td></tr><tr><td>Confetti Cake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>490</td><td>Slightly richer cake flavor</td></tr><tr><td>S'mores Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>500</td><td>More complex campfire flavor</td></tr><tr><td>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Year-round, lower price</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (4.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (5.29) at 460 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

